@startuml zero_trust_gates
!pragma layout smetana
!include _style.puml
title Zero Trust — three gates, never trust, always verify

rectangle "**Gate 1 — Identity**\nPRESENT-80 challenge/response\nsingle-use nonce, 30 s TTL\n+ source-IP pin" as G1 #fdecf1
rectangle "**Gate 2 — Continuous verification**\nevery task updates trust\nT = αR + βB + γH − δA\nanomaly gate A ≥ 0.5 runs beside it" as G2 #fdecf1
rectangle "**Gate 3 — Graduated response**\nfull rate → rate-limit → quarantine\nenforced as OpenFlow rules" as G3 #fdecf1

rectangle "Device admitted" as OK
rectangle "403 auth_denied\nip_pin · bad_response · nonce_expired" as NO
rectangle "Node keeps serving" as SERVE
rectangle "Node isolated in the data plane\nprobation lets it return" as ISO

G1 -right-> OK   : verified
G1 -down->  NO   : refused
OK -down->  G2
G2 -right-> SERVE : trusted
G2 -down->  G3    : T < 0.30  **or**  A ≥ 0.50
G3 -right-> ISO
ISO -up->   G2    : probation, 5 s

note bottom of G2
  Two independent rails. Either one alone
  misses attackers — see Finding 1.
end note
@enduml
